  "id": "beta-coefficient",
  "term": "beta coefficient",
  "definition": "A beta coefficient is a statistical number used to describe how strongly one variable is related to another and in which direction. In this context, a standardized beta coefficient below zero indicates that more television watching was associated with lower cognitive scores.",
